<title>GERMANY: Welteke - pointless to discuss German EMU failure.</title>
<headline>Welteke - pointless to discuss German EMU failure.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank council member Ernst Welteke said on Friday it was pointless to discuss whether Germany would fail to meet Maastricht Treaty criteria, saying such talk was &quot;absolute humbug&quot;.</p>
<p>He said Germany already met criteria on monetary stability, central bank independence and low inflation.</p>
<p>&quot;And we have the possability of fulfiling the fiscal criteria,&quot; Welteke said, adding that such criteria were not exact numbers targets. &quot;The issue of sustainability is the critical factor,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom + 49 69 756525</p>
